{"files":[{"content":"#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <omp.h>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint main() {\n    int n, m;\n    if (!(cin >> n >> m)) return 0;\n\n    vector<vector<bool>> blockedCells(n, vector<bool>(n, false));\n    for (int c = 0; c < m; ++c) {\n        int i, j;\n        cin >> i >> j;\n        blockedCells[i][j] = true;\n    }\n\n    vector<int> dp(n, 0);\n    if (!blockedCells[0][0]) dp[0] = 1;\n    for (int j = 1; j < n; ++j) {\n        dp[j] = blockedCells[0][j] ? 0 : dp[j - 1];\n    }\n\n    if (n > 1) {\n#pragma omp parallel\n        {\n            const int threads = omp_get_num_threads();\n            const int tid = omp_get_thread_num();\n            const int begin = static_cast<int>((static_cast<long long>(n) * tid) / threads);\n            const int end = static_cast<int>((static_cast<long long>(n) * (tid + 1)) / threads);\n            static vector<int> tails;\n            static vector<int> firstBlocked;\n            static vector<int> offsets;\n\n#pragma omp single\n            {\n                tails.resize(threads);\n                firstBlocked.resize(threads);\n                offsets.resize(threads);\n            }\n\n            for (int i = 1; i < n; ++i) {\n                int value = 0;\n                int first = end;\n                for (int j = begin; j < end; ++j) {\n                    if (blockedCells[i][j]) {\n                        value = 0;\n                        if (first == end) first = j;\n                    } else {\n                        value += dp[j];\n                        if (value >= MOD) value -= MOD;\n                    }\n                    dp[j] = value;\n                }\n                tails[tid] = value;\n                firstBlocked[tid] = first;\n\n#pragma omp barrier\n#pragma omp single\n                {\n                    int carry = 0;\n                    for (int t = 0; t < threads; ++t) {\n                        offsets[t] = carry;\n                        if (firstBlocked[t] == static_cast<int>((static_cast<long long>(n) * (t + 1)) / threads)) {\n                            carry += tails[t];\n                            if (carry >= MOD) carry -= MOD;\n                        } else {\n                            carry = tails[t];\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n\n                const int stop = firstBlocked[tid];\n                const int offset = offsets[tid];\n                if (offset != 0) {\n                    for (int j = begin; j < stop; ++j) {\n                        int valueWithCarry = dp[j] + offset;\n                        dp[j] = valueWithCarry >= MOD ? valueWithCarry - MOD : valueWithCarry;\n                    }\n                }\n#pragma omp barrier\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << dp[n - 1] << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/solution.cpp"}],"hypothesis":"A persistent OpenMP team can parallelize each DP row by computing independent segmented prefix recurrences, then propagating only one carry per thread segment; removing the original full-row copy also reduces memory traffic.","notes":"The segmented recurrence preserves obstacle resets and modular arithmetic for every grid size, including n=1.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Replace two rolling rows and their per-row copy with one in-place DP row.","Use persistent OpenMP segmented work sharing and a serial four-element carry scan per row.","Correct the n=1 result through direct first-row initialization."]}